{
  "title": "Kniest Dysplasia",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4098/kniest-dysplasia",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 17 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Kniest's Dysplasia is a rare congenital disorder caused by a defect in the COL2A1 gene leading to abnormal Type II collagen. Patients present with a form of disproportionate short-trunk dwarfism with characteristic features such as ocular abnormalities, cleft palate, and hearing loss.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made based on family history associated with typical radiographic and clinical features. No commercially available diagnostic test exists due to the variety of genetic mutations.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment involves a multidisciplinary approach to address orthopedic manifestations, fascial abnormalities, and ocular abnormalities.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Genetics**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**autosomal dominant**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "defect in COL2A1 (missense, splice or deletion)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "defect leads to abnormal **Type II collagen, chondrocyte degeneration, cytoplasmic inclusions**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
